nodecode-tenuo is a rewrite of tenuo-ai's tenuo-ai/hermes-tenuo:

  https://github.com/tenuo-ai/hermes-tenuo
  commit 8bce830c5df9dcd06d16688a954146d8ed0c0c562
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Tenuo AI (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the Hermes plugin's per-call authorization as one Nodecode cell —
the warrant (tools and argument constraints, with an expiry), the check before
every tool call with the refusal handed back to the model as the call's
failure, the local JSONL audit log of every decision, and read-only access to
the policy for the model (tenuo_check, tenuo_audit) and the operator (/tenuo).

Left out: the tenuo Rust SDK and its Ed25519 warrants, which no cell can link
without bundling a compiled library. A warrant here is a JSON file the
operator writes, and the integrity check is an HMAC-SHA256 of that file kept
beside it as <warrant>.sig under a key named by key_env (`/tenuo sign` writes
it) — the same "a tampered warrant is a refusal, not a quiet promotion" rule,
in the cryptography a Lisp image already has. Also left out: the control-plane
stream (TENUO_CONNECT_TOKEN), which was that SDK's; minting and key rotation,
which were `hermes-tenuo mint`; per-session and per-gateway-user warrants,
which needed the original's session registry; and kanban per-task warrants and
the auto-block of a task on denial, which were the Hermes kanban's — Nodecode
sessions have no such board, so a denial here is the call's failure and an
audit line.
